decision: changes-requested

Two high-severity blockers remain:

- **N40 — incomplete start-state checks**, `validate.go:1447`: full runs check submodule initialization and hidden index flags only at the end. A check can pass against absent or hidden material, restore the committed state, and produce a reusable `material_clean` record.
- **N41 — cleanliness sampled after planning**, `validate.go:1158`: uncommitted manifests can influence module discovery and be restored before `startedClean` is sampled, without moving HEAD.
- **N42 — low follow-up**, `validate.go:1616`: reports still present carried checks as executed commands without their original head and time. This remains tracked as F2.

These blockers are source-traced; new synthetic reproductions were unavailable because scratch-directory creation was denied. Existing focused tests, race tests, delivery-parser tests, publication-guard tests and `go vet` passed. The full validation reruns were invoked but had not completed at conclusion; their tool dispositions below cite the supplied sealed canonical evidence.

Applied the review workflow and security, backend-Go, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. The checkout remained unchanged; no attestation was recorded.

